"Let $N_{1/(2r-1)}(d)$ denote the maximum number of equiangular lines in $\\mathbb{R}^d$ with common angle $\\arccos \\frac{1}{2r-1}$, where $r\\geq 2$ is an integer. **Asymptotic equiangular-lines conjecture.** For every integer $r\\geq 2$,\n\n$$\nN_{1/(2r-1)}(d)=\\frac{r}{r-1}d+O(1)\n$$\n\nas $d$ tends to infinity. The construction preceding the conjecture gives the matching lower bound, and the cited results suggest that it is sharp; the conjectured asymptotic upper bound remains open."